.TH BOOTSTRAP_HEARTBEAT_MONITOR.SH 1 "2026-10-06" "mu2edaq-heartbeatmonitor t01.00.00" "Mu2e DAQ Manual"
.SH NAME
bootstrap_heartbeat_monitor.sh \- create the monitor virtual environment
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ./bootstrap_heartbeat_monitor.sh
.SH DESCRIPTION
Creates a Python virtual environment
.I venv
in the
.B current working directory
with
.BR "python3 \-m venv" ,
installs
.I ../mu2edaq\-discovery
in editable mode if that directory exists, installs
.IR requirements.txt
(Flask and PyYAML), and creates the directories
.IR data ,
.I logs
and
.IR config .
.PP
All paths are relative to the working directory, not to the script, so it
must be run from the package directory.
It has no
.BR "set \-e" :
a failed step does not stop it, and it always prints a success message.
Inspect the output.
These limitations are tracked in GitHub issue #8.
.PP
The name differs from the
.B bootstrap.sh
used by most sibling packages.
.SH OPTIONS
None.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ./venv
Virtual environment used by
.BR start\-mu2edaq\-heartbeatmonitor.sh (1).
.TP
.I ./requirements.txt
Python dependencies.
.TP
.I ../mu2edaq\-discovery
Optional sibling checkout providing service discovery.
.SH EXIT STATUS
The status of the last command, normally 0, whether or not earlier steps
succeeded.
.SH EXAMPLES
.RS 4
.nf
cd ~/mu2edaq\-main/mu2edaq\-heartbeatmonitor
\&./bootstrap_heartbeat_monitor.sh
venv/bin/python \-c 'import flask, yaml; print("ok")'
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR start\-mu2edaq\-heartbeatmonitor.sh (1),
.BR heartbeat_monitor.py (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Mu2e DAQ Group, Fermi National Accelerator Laboratory.
